{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2992","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2992","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2992\",\"parent_revision\":\"bc8ef6b1dd3bbdbe1fe09a0e6a5b55796fbd767c\",\"root_revision\":\"435b08ecbb5cc90e668c6b42342beb6ee94c23d3b4838d452ae7229a88ce2cc5\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P0\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: 2026-08-19\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nInvoking `/dh:work-backlog-item create -- \\\"<text>\\\"` failed both times it was attempted in this session, with:\\n\\n```\\nError: Shell command failed for pattern \\\"!`...`\\\": [stderr]\\n(eval):1: permission denied: ../..\\n```\\n\\n`plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/SKILL.md:9` contains `` !`node \\\"${CLAUDE_SKILL_DIR}/scripts/get-gate-token.mjs\\\"` ``. That line was added by commit `11ad9145` (2026-05-18) \u2014 unrelated to and predating this session's own PR #2981 work on this file.\\n\\nRunning the script directly from the repo root (`node plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/scripts/get-gate-token.mjs`) succeeds and prints a token \u2014 so the script itself is not broken in isolation. The failure is specific to the harness's `` !`...` `` execution of this line at skill-invocation time, where `${CLAUDE_SKILL_DIR}` substitution or the resulting working-directory/exec context differs from a plain repo-root shell invocation. The literal string `../..` appearing in the error suggests something in that resolved path or command is being treated as an executable target rather than an argument, but this has not been root-caused \u2014 do not assume the standalone success generalizes to the actual failure condition.\\n\\nImpact: this specific slash-command entry point to the skill is currently unusable in at least this environment. Workaround this session was to read the skill's reference files directly and call the `backlog_add` MCP tool by hand \u2014 not proof the underlying invocation defect is fixed, just that it was bypassed.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer relying on this plugin**, I want to **/dh:work-backlog-item create invocation fails: get-gate-token.mjs errors \\\"permission denied: ../..\\\" via harness shell injection** so that **the tool works correctly and reliably**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Observed directly, 2026-08-19, twice in a row (including after /reload-plugins)\\n- **Priority**: P0\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-19\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"17c7a5aa20aa25682f5fdf111870fe2e1e61fbfa8c24c029d444fbc0b8431bcf\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPiIkTA\"}"}